    "updated_at": "2020-03-03T10:04:38Z",
    "body": "If we add a new value to type, how would you check support without (potentially) spinning up a worker? The suggestions without `terminate()` only work for this one-off transition. (And even if we did add it, those wanting to support earlier browsers with module worker support would end up with an even more convoluted check.)\r\n\r\n(It's unfortunate that t sorts after n, otherwise you could throw from the name getter to avoid instantiation.)",
